# UI Design Essentials

## Color System

Use semantic color classes only:

| Purpose      | Background    | Text                        |
|-------------|---------------|----------------------------|
| Primary     | bg-primary    | text-primary-foreground    |
| Default     | bg-default    | text-default-foreground    |
| Background  | bg-background | text-foreground            |
| Muted       | bg-muted      | text-muted-foreground      |
| Destructive | bg-destructive| text-destructive-foreground|

## Typography

### Font Sizes
- `text-xs`: Labels, metadata
- `text-sm`: Secondary text, errors
- `text-base`: Default body text
- `text-lg`: Page titles (content-heavy only)

### Font Weights
- `font-normal`: Default text
- `font-semibold`: Headings, important labels

### Heading Patterns
```jsx
// Main Page (H1)
<div className="h-80 pt-10 flex flex-col px-10">
  <h1 className="font-semibold mb-5">Title</h1>
</div>

// Section (H2, H3)
<div className="px-10 h-40 flex flex-col justify-center">
  <h2 className="font-semibold">{title}</h2>
</div>
```

## Spacing

Prefer multiples of 5 here (so no h-4 or w-9, instead h-5 or h-10)

### Key Classes
- Tight: `p-2`, `gap-2`
- Standard: `p-5`, `gap-5`
- Large: `p-10`, `gap-10`

### Heights
- `h-20`: Standard row
- `h-40`: Double height
- `h-80`: Quadruple height (page headers)

## Component Patterns

### Buttons
```jsx
<Button variant="default">Default</Button>
<Button variant="primary">Primary Action</Button>
<Button variant="outline" size="icon">
  <Icon className="size-4" />
</Button>
```

### Forms
```jsx
<div className="space-y-2">
  <Label>Label</Label>
  <Input placeholder="Input" />
</div>
```

### Cards
```jsx
<div className="bg-card text-card-foreground p-5 rounded-lg border">
  <h3 className="font-semibold">Title</h3>
  <p className="text-muted-foreground">Content</p>
</div>
```

## Best Practices

1. Use semantic colors only
2. Maintain consistent spacing
3. Follow row system for fixed-height sections
4. Test in both light/dark modes
5. Use appropriate text sizes
6. Keep headings in fixed-height containers 